vaporOS NuttX patch: rp2040-crashdump-waveshare

Problem:   With no UART and no debugger, a crash leaves nothing to look at; the
           USB console dies with the chip.
Evidence:  Early crashes (stack overflows in tbx) were invisible until a record
           of PC/LR/registers survived the reset.
Fix:       board_crashdump() stores pc, lr, sp, xpsr, r0-r3, r12, the task's
           stack bounds, name, file, line and message in a struct at the top
           of SRAM (0x2003ff00), then the board resets. After it comes back
           up, `xd 2003ff00 96` dumps the record. It lives in SRAM3, not
           SRAM4/5, because the bootrom uses SRAM4/5 while rebooting.
Upstream:  MAYBE. The mechanism (CONFIG_BOARD_CRASHDUMP_CUSTOM hook) is
           upstream already; this is just a RAM-record implementation for one
           board. Could generalise as a "crash record in RAM" helper.

Apply: git -C ../nuttx apply ../vaporOS/patches/nuttx/rp2040-crashdump-waveshare.patch   (setup.sh does this)

diff --git a/boards/arm/rp2040/waveshare-rp2040-zero/src/Make.defs b/boards/arm/rp2040/waveshare-rp2040-zero/src/Make.defs
index f2a92e8ced..865abfca4d 100644
--- a/boards/arm/rp2040/waveshare-rp2040-zero/src/Make.defs
+++ b/boards/arm/rp2040/waveshare-rp2040-zero/src/Make.defs
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/Make.defs
 
 CSRCS = rp2040_boardinitialize.c
+CSRCS += rp2040_crashdump.c
 CSRCS += rp2040_bringup.c
 
